    <label>Saxons</label>
    <description>Sea raiders from the coasts of the North Sea, between the Elbe and the Rhine, whose keels have harried the Saxon Shore of Britain and Gaul for a hundred years. Now that the legions have left Britain, Saxon war bands under leaders like Hengest and Horsa come as hired swords and stay as conquerors. They fight on foot behind a wall of painted shields: warriors with the long seax that gave them their name, axemen, javelin and axe throwers, wolf-coated madmen and their war hounds, with only a few horsemen. They keep the old gods, Woden, Thunor and Tiw, and they are at war with Rome.</description>
